      "id": "claim_c10e8f242217432ead85fce0cc376b0a",
      "statement": "sandbox-worker.js captures CheerpJ output by monkeypatching console.log/error/warn/info to append to a captured string (no DOM exists in a Worker, so CheerpJ stdout/stderr land on the worker's own console), then parses sentinel-delimited output: it reports runtime-error if ERR_PREFIX is present, slices stdout between OUT_BEGIN/OUT_END stripping all leading/trailing blank lines (because CheerpJ's console bridge doesn't preserve exact newline counts), collects every RET_PREFIX line into returns, and a non-zero runExit with no OUT_BEGIN is a runtime-error; otherwise posts { status: 'ok', stdout, returns }. Thrown exceptions become { status: 'error', message }.",
